{"text":"MODEL_FEEDBACK_JSON:
{
  "positive_alignment_reasons": [
    "The HDMI cable and wired earbuds connect with my past interest in display connections and a headset with a microphone, although neither gives me a clear reason to replace what I have.",
    "The mouse and USB 3.0 drive fit my practical computer setup interests; they would make sense if I needed a replacement mouse or more storage."
  ],
  "negative_misalignment_reasons": [
    "The streaming devices and Echo products serve entertainment or voice-assistant needs that my purchases do not suggest I currently have.",
    "My tablet mount was an accessory for using a device, so recommending a new tablet assumes a replacement need I have not expressed."
  ],
  "overgeneralized_signals": [
    "The recommendations seem to treat an interest in computer connections as an interest in electronics generally.",
    "Several widely purchased devices appear despite having little connection to the specific practical tasks behind my purchases."
  ],
  "missing_or_underweighted_signals": [
    "My latest purchase addressed wired network connectivity, following earlier purchases that added wireless access and USB ports; solving connection needs matters more to me than adding entertainment devices.",
    "My purchases are infrequent and serve specific purposes. Even a related accessory needs a clear use and the right connections before I would choose it."
  ],
  "summary_diagnosis": "The recommendations partly recognize my interest in practical computer accessories but stretch it into a broader desire for electronics without identifying a current need."
}"}
